SUMMARY:The Art of Kokedama: Japanese Moss Ball Planting
DESCRIPTION:With Cathrina of Cat Hawk Gardens\, “The Kokedama Mama”\nDiscover the Japanese art of kokedama—living plant arrangements wrapped in moss. Guided by Cathrina of Cat Hawk Gardens\, you’ll explore this mindful practice of balance\, beauty\, and simplicity while creating your own kokedama to take home. \nIn this workshop you’ll:\n* Learn traditional techniques for forming and binding moss balls\n* Make your own kokedama to take home\n* Gain skills to continue creating on your own \nAll supplies provided. Includes a grounding Self-Breema movement practice to connect body and mind.
URL:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/event/the-art-of-kokedama-japanese-moss-ball-planting/
LOCATION:Gather Sebastopol\, 122 N. Main Street\, Sebastopol\, 95472
CATEGORIES:Skill-Building Workshop
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Kokedama.png
END:VEVENT
